 "note": "hands v3c (2026-10-14), for hands_v3c_post.py (field hands_v3b_field.py, remesh toe_remesh.py), appended after P-pawrefine1 in place of hands v3b. Coordinator review of v3b (2026-10-14): zigzag pleats in the valleys between the toes at normal size (side and below), and a soft crease along the palm pad's lower edge; shapes, separations and claw seating to stay as v3b. Field, toes, claws and mover exactly as v3b, except the palm pad's blend radius .010 (v3b .006), which takes the crease off its lower edge. Then toeRemesh, per paw: the skin's faces below z -.158 in the toe zone (|x| above .275, y -.16 to -.04, z above -.25) are copied, closed, voxel-remeshed at .0007, cut .001 below z -.162 and bridged to the skin cut at z -.162 (bridge_loops without merge: the loops have unequal counts); every new face takes the nearest old face's material; every new vertex is projected exactly onto the hands field and Taubin-smoothed 10 passes (projected back each pass); the skin just above the cut (blendH .027) is blended onto the field so the seam leaves no step. Development variants v3h and v3i in untracked anatomy-fixes/work/08-hands/specs (this is v3i, field from gen4.py). World units, +y back.",
